{
  "project": {
    "name": "Jinbei (Top)",
    "slug": "jinbei-top",
    "version": "0.1.0",
    "engine": "fc",
    "description": {
      "en": "The jacket of the traditional Japanese summer set (jinbei), worn at home and at festivals: a light, open, kimono-cut top with wide dropped sleeves that closes with inner and outer side ties. This cartridge drafts the jacket in the straight-seam idiom of Japanese garment construction (back on fold + two overlapping fronts + wide sleeves); the sashiko stitching and aizome dyeing are the maker's. A soft-goods garment — no hardware. Traditionally paired with matching shorts. FC-200 long-tail (heritage). Offered with respect for the living tradition.\n\nOfficial visualizer and configurator: Fashion Cabinet",
      "es": "La chaqueta del conjunto de verano tradicional japonés (jinbei), usado en casa y en festivales: un top ligero, abierto y de corte kimono con mangas anchas caídas que cierra con lazos internos y externos al costado. Este cartucho traza la chaqueta en el estilo de costuras rectas de la confección japonesa (espalda al canto + dos frentes traslapados + mangas anchas); el bordado sashiko y el teñido aizome pertenecen a quien elabora. Una prenda textil — sin herrajes. Tradicionalmente combinado con pantalón corto a juego. Cola larga FC-200 (patrimonio). Ofrecido con respeto por la tradición viva.\n\nVisualizador y configurador oficial: Fashion Cabinet"
    },
    "difficulty": "intermediate",
    "tags": [
      "jinbei",
      "heritage",
      "japanese",
      "kimono-cut",
      "summer",
      "commons",
      "made-to-measure"
    ],
    "attribution": {
      "author": "Innovaciones MADFAM",
      "license": "LicenseRef-FC1-pending",
      "lineage": [
        {
          "source": "Original draft for Fashion Cabinet",
          "license": "original"
        }
      ]
    }
  },
